      "content": "MAGNETISM"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Magnetic field lines emerge from the North Pole and terminate at the South Pole outside a magnet, forming continuous closed loops.",
        "Magnetic field strength (B) around a straight conductor is directly proportional to current (I) and inversely proportional to distance (r).",
        "Fleming's Left Hand Rule determines the direction of mechanical force in an Electric Motor.",
        "Fleming's Right Hand Rule determines the direction of induced current in an Electric Generator.",
        "Electromagnets are temporary magnets made with a soft iron core, whereas permanent magnets are made of steel or alloys like Alnico."
      ],
      "id": "ahtg3ig"
    },
    {
